  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1996, in the Brazilian town of Varginha, a creature said to have been captured after a crash was taken while still alive first to a hospital called Regional and then to another called Humanitas. The filmmaker James Fox, who investigated the case and talked to its witnesses, tells Michels this, saying 'we knew for decades' that it went 'initially alive to Regional' and then to Humanitas. If true, it would mean a living non-human being passed through ordinary Brazilian hospitals."
}
